    <br><div class="row"><div class="col-12 col-lg-3 staff-profile"><div data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#profileModal_20"><div class="text-center staff-profile-image ratio ratio-1x1"><img src="/files/endorsed-candidates-photos/Mike_Levin_Pic_600x750.jpg" alt="Mike Levin" class="img-fluid rounded-circle" /></div>
                    <div class="text-center staff-profile-name"><h5>Mike Levin</h5></div>
                    <div class="text-center staff-profile-position"><p><em>United States Representative, 49TH District</em></p></div></div>
                
                    <div class="modal fade" id="profileModal_20" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="profileModalLabel" aria-hidden="true"><div class="modal-dialog modal-lg modal-fullscreen-sm-down"><div class="modal-content"><div class="modal-header"><h1 class="modal-title fs-5" id="profileModalLabel">Mike Levin</h1>
                        <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button></div>
                      <div class="modal-body"><div class="container-fluid"><div class="row"><div class="col-12 col-lg-4"><img src="/files/endorsed-candidates-photos/Mike_Levin_Pic_600x750.jpg" alt="Mike Levin" class="img-fluid" /></div>
                                <div class="col-12 col-lg-8"><p><strong>Position:</strong> United States Representative, 49TH District</p><div>Currently serving in his fourth term in Congress, Mike is a member of the powerful House Committee on Appropriations, where he serves on the Subcommittees on Energy and Water Development and Related Agencies and Military Construction, Veterans Affairs, and Related Agencies. Throughout his time in Congress, more than 35 of his bills have been signed into law by presidents of both parties.&nbsp;<div><br></div><div>Mike was raised in South Orange County, by a MexicanAmerican mother and a Jewish-American father. He is the grandson of Mexican immigrants on his mother’s side.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Since flipping the 49th district from red to blue in 2018, Mike’s top priorities in Congress have been combating climate change, protecting our coast, protecting our natural resources, supporting our small businesses, coastal communities, schools, and working to strengthen benefits and services for our veterans. Mike has also been a champion for a woman’s right to make her own healthcare decisions, and for the LGBTQIA community.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Since taking office in 2019, Mike is proud to have secured over $1 billion in federal funding for the district. For a detailed list of the funding, please visit:&nbsp; https://www.mikelevin.org/#funding&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>The independent and nonpartisan Center for Effective Lawmaking rates Mike among the top five percent most&nbsp; effective lawmakers in the House of Representatives.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>The Veterans of Foreign Wars (VFW) named Mike Levin their 2024 Legislator of the Year because of his tireless and effective advocacy on behalf of veterans and their families. https://www.mik
1000
elevin.org/</div></div></div></div></div></div>
                      <div class="modal-footer"><button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-bs-dismiss="modal">Close</button></div></div></div></div>
                </div><div class="col-12 col-lg-3 staff-profile"><div data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#profileModal_21"><div class="text-center staff-profile-image ratio ratio-1x1"><img src="/files/endorsed-candidates-photos/MarniVonWilpert_Pic_600x750.jpg" alt="Marni von Wilpert" class="img-fluid rounded-circle" /></div>
                    <div class="text-center staff-profile-name"><h5>Marni von Wilpert</h5></div>
                    <div class="text-center staff-profile-position"><p><em>House of Representatives in 48th District</em></p></div></div>
                
                    <div class="modal fade" id="profileModal_21" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="profileModalLabel" aria-hidden="true"><div class="modal-dialog modal-lg modal-fullscreen-sm-down"><div class="modal-content"><div class="modal-header"><h1 class="modal-title fs-5" id="profileModalLabel">Marni von Wilpert</h1>
                        <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button></div>
                      <div class="modal-body"><div class="container-fluid"><div class="row"><div class="col-12 col-lg-4"><img src="/files/endorsed-candidates-photos/MarniVonWilpert_Pic_600x750.jpg" alt="Marni von Wilpert" class="img-fluid" /></div>
                                <div class="col-12 col-lg-8"><p><strong>Position:</strong> House of Representatives in 48th District</p><div>Marni von Wilpert is a San Diego City Councilmember, lifelong public servant, and former prosecutor who flipped San Diego’s most conservative city council seat blue – and she’s ready to do it again in Congress.&nbsp;<div><br></div><div>Raised in North County San Diego and a Peace Corps alum, Marni has spent her career fighting for working families — from helping write the Protect The Right To Organize Act (PRO Act) in Congress to prosecuting price gougers, polluters, and wage theft back home.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>On the City Council, she authored California’s first ghost gun ban, launched affordable housing grants for teachers, raised wages, reduced emergency response times, expanded access to clean energy, and fought to combat the opioid crisis while protecting taxpayers and strengthening public safety.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Marni is running for Congress to tackle the skyrocketing cost of living, protect reproductive freedom, defend equal rights, and make Washington work for working families — not just the wealthy few.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>With a proven record of service, results, and winning tough races, Marni is the battle-tested fighter we need to flip CA-48, beat MAGA extremist Jim Desmond, and lower costs for Californians.&nbsp;</div></div></div></div></div></div>
                      <div class="modal-footer"><button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-bs-dismiss="modal">Close</button></div></div></div></div>
                </div><div class="col-12 col-lg-3 staff-profile"><div data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#profileModal_22"><div class="text-center staff-profile-image ratio ratio-1x1"><img src="/files/endorsed-candidates-photos/Martha_Abraham_Pic_600x750.jpg" alt="Martha Abraham" class="img-fluid rounded-circle" /></div>
                    <div class="text-center staff-profile-name"><h5>Martha Abraham</h5></div>
                    <div class="text-center staff-profile-position"><p><em>San Diego City Council, District 4</em></p></div></div>
                
                    <div class="modal fade" id="profileModal_22" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="profileModalLabel" aria-hidden="true"><div class="modal-dialog modal-lg modal-fullscreen-sm-down"><div class="modal-content"><div class="modal-header"><h1 class="modal-title fs-5" id="profileModalLabel">Martha Abraham</h1>
                        <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dism
1000
iss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button></div>
                      <div class="modal-body"><div class="container-fluid"><div class="row"><div class="col-12 col-lg-4"><img src="/files/endorsed-candidates-photos/Martha_Abraham_Pic_600x750.jpg" alt="Martha Abraham" class="img-fluid" /></div>
                                <div class="col-12 col-lg-8"><p><strong>Position:</strong> San Diego City Council, District 4</p><div>A healthy environment is essential to the health, safety, and quality of life of our community. Protecting our environment means protecting the health, quality of life, and future of every neighborhood. My campaign is grounded in the belief that every community deserves access to parks, open space, clean air, and resilient infrastructure that can withstand the impacts of climate change.<div><br></div><div>Communities of color have borne a disproportionate share of pollution while receiving fewer environmental investments. I am committed to advancing environmental justice by ensuring these neighborhoods have a voice in decisions that affect their health and environment.</div><div><br></div><div>As a City Council candidate, I will champion policies that preserve our natural areas, expand parks and green spaces, and invest in climate resilience through sustainable infrastructure, urban tree canopy, and responsible land-use planning. Protecting our open spaces and preparing for a changing climate are essential to&nbsp; creating healthier, stronger communities for future generations.</div><div><br></div><div>With gratitude and determination, www.martha4sandiego.com</div></div></div></div></div></div>
                      <div class="modal-footer"><button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-bs-dismiss="modal">Close</button></div></div></div></div>
                </div><div class="col-12 col-lg-3 staff-profile"><div data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#profileModal_23"><div class="text-center staff-profile-image ratio ratio-1x1"><img src="/files/endorsed-candidates-photos/Antonio_Martinez_Pic_600x750.jpg" alt="Antonio Martinez" class="img-fluid rounded-circle" /></div>
                    <div class="text-center staff-profile-name"><h5>Antonio Martinez</h5></div>
                    <div class="text-center staff-profile-position"><p><em>San Diego City Council District 8</em></p></div></div>
                
                    <div class="modal fade" id="profileModal_23" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="profileModalLabel" aria-hidden="true"><div class="modal-dialog modal-lg modal-fullscreen-sm-down"><div class="modal-content"><div class="modal-header"><h1 class="modal-title fs-5" id="profileModalLabel">Antonio Martinez</h1>
                        <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button></div>
                      <div class="modal-body"><div class="container-fluid"><div class="row"><div class="col-12 col-lg-4"><img src="/files/endorsed-candidates-photos/Antonio_Martinez_Pic_600x750.jpg" alt="Antonio Martinez" class="img-fluid" /></div>
                                <div class="col-12 col-lg-8"><p><strong>Position:</strong> San Diego City Council District 8</p><div>For Antonio Martinez, District 8 isn’t just where he lives, it’s home. A lifelong resident of the community, Antonio was raised by his grandmother, who taught him the values that continue to guide him today: work hard, stay humble, and never forget where you come from.<div><br></div><div>Antonio became the first in his family to attend college, graduating from the University of Pennsylvania. Although his education took him across the country, his heart and commitment remained with the community that raised him. He returned home determined to use his opportunities to serve others and help open doors for the next generation. Antonio began his career as a healthcare educator at the Nestor Community Clinic, working directly with local families and helping connect them with vital information and resources. He later continued his public service through congressional work, he
1000
lping residents navigate government and ensuring their voices were heard.</div><div><br></div><div>As a Governing Board Member of the San Ysidro School District, Antonio has worked to give local children the opportunities they deserve. He has helped strengthen educational programs, advocate for improvements to aging school facilities, and promote greater transparency and accountability.</div><div><br></div><div>Antonio’s story is rooted in the same neighborhoods, families, and experiences that make District 8 special. He understands both the challenges our communities face and their incredible potential. Now, Antonio is running for San Diego City Council District 8 to give back to the community that gave him so much and to make sure every family, every neighborhood, and every voice has a seat at the table.</div></div></div></div></div></div>
                      <div class="modal-footer"><button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-bs-dismiss="modal">Close</button></div></div></div></div>
                </div><div class="col-12 col-lg-3 staff-profile"><div data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#profileModal_24"><div class="text-center staff-profile-image ratio ratio-1x1"><img src="/files/endorsed-candidates-photos/Meghan_O_Ryan_Spieker_600x750.jpg" alt="Meghan O&#x2019;Ryan Spieker" class="img-fluid rounded-circle" /></div>
                    <div class="text-center staff-profile-name"><h5>Meghan O&#x2019;Ryan Spieker</h5></div>
                    <div class="text-center staff-profile-position"><p><em>Del Mar City Council</em></p></div></div>
                
                    <div class="modal fade" id="profileModal_24" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="profileModalLabel" aria-hidden="true"><div class="modal-dialog modal-lg modal-fullscreen-sm-down"><div class="modal-content"><div class="modal-header"><h1 class="modal-title fs-5" id="profileModalLabel">Meghan O&#x2019;Ryan Spieker</h1>
                        <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button></div>
                      <div class="modal-body"><div class="container-fluid"><div class="row"><div class="col-12 col-lg-4"><img src="/files/endorsed-candidates-photos/Meghan_O_Ryan_Spieker_600x750.jpg" alt="Meghan O&#x2019;Ryan Spieker" class="img-fluid" /></div>
                                <div class="col-12 col-lg-8"><p><strong>Position:</strong> Del Mar City Council</p><div>Meghan O’Ryan Spieker is a Del Mar Planning Commissioner, former business litigator, and nonprofit leader with a longstanding commitment to protecting California’s natural resources and communities.<div><br></div><div>For more than 10 years, Meghan has served on the board of the California Wildlife Officers Foundation (CalWOF), which provides citizen support to the wildlife officers who protect California’s lands, waters, and wildlife. California wildlife officers are on the front lines of protecting our environment, enforcing laws against poaching and other environmental crimes, and responding to threats to our natural resources. Meghan is proud to support their work and the important role they play as environmental stewards.</div><div><br></div><div>Before entering nonprofit leadership, Meghan practiced business litigation for 16 years at major international law firms, representing public companies and their officers and directors in complex disputes. She subsequently served as Founding Board Chair of Free to Thrive, a San Diego nonprofit providing legal services to survivors of human trafficking; as a Trustee of Francis Parker School; and in leadership roles, including President, with Teen Volunteers in Action.</div><div><br></div><div>As a Planning Commissioner, Meghan strives to serve with rigor, courtesy, and equanimity. She believes Del Mar can meet the challenges of growth while protecting the community’s character, natural environment, and long-term sustainability.</div><div><br></div><div>Meghan lives in Del Mar with her husband and four sons. She earned her undergraduate degree from UC Berkeley and her
1000
 law degree, with honors, from Georgetown.</div></div></div></div></div></div>
                      <div class="modal-footer"><button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-bs-dismiss="modal">Close</button></div></div></div></div>
                </div><div class="col-12 col-lg-3 staff-profile"><div data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#profileModal_25"><div class="text-center staff-profile-image ratio ratio-1x1"><img src="/files/endorsed-candidates-photos/JAS_GREWAL_Pic_600x750.jpg" alt="Jas Grewal" class="img-fluid rounded-circle" /></div>
                    <div class="text-center staff-profile-name"><h5>Jas Grewal</h5></div>
                    <div class="text-center staff-profile-position"><p><em>Del Mar City Council</em></p></div></div>
                
                    <div class="modal fade" id="profileModal_25" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="profileModalLabel" aria-hidden="true"><div class="modal-dialog modal-lg modal-fullscreen-sm-down"><div class="modal-content"><div class="modal-header"><h1 class="modal-title fs-5" id="profileModalLabel">Jas Grewal</h1>
                        <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button></div>
                      <div class="modal-body"><div class="container-fluid"><div class="row"><div class="col-12 col-lg-4"><img src="/files/endorsed-candidates-photos/JAS_GREWAL_Pic_600x750.jpg" alt="Jas Grewal" class="img-fluid" /></div>
                                <div class="col-12 col-lg-8"><p><strong>Position:</strong> Del Mar City Council</p><div>Del Mar is at a turning point with important issues that must be properly handled.<div><br></div><div>This election will decide if we follow the Community Plan that has successfully guided Del Mar for more than 50 years or choose expensive ideas that could create unreasonable debt and weaken City essential services.&nbsp;&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>As a 34-year resident of Del Mar, being a Planning Commissioner for the last 3 years, a former member of the City’s Finance Committee for 8 years, Chair of the Citizen’s Taskforce for the 6th housing Element, and Del Mar’s representative at the Clean Energy Alliance Advisory Board, I understand the issues Del Mar is facing.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>As a retired banker, I know the importance of careful planning and financial discipline. Borrowing millions of dollars to speed up projects we are already paying for over time could put Del Mar at serious risk, especially if the economy slows down.</div><div><br></div><div>If elected, I will help rebuild relationships with regional agencies, find practical ways to meet State housing rules, support moving the train off the bluffs without tunneling under homes or businesses, protect our fast emergency response times, improve wildfire and sea-level-rise safety without managed retreat, and preserve Del Mar’s special character.</div><div><br></div><div>I believe City Council members should be good stewards of our land and put residents’ interests first. I will be a leader Del Mar deserves serving with honesty, ethics, and integrity.</div><div><br></div><div>Please see Jas4DelMar.com for my civic experience, business background and decades of involvement. I would be grateful for your support.</div></div></div></div></div></div>
                      <div class="modal-footer"><button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-bs-dismiss="modal">Close</button></div></div></div></div>
                </div><div class="col-12 col-lg-3 staff-profile"><div data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#profileModal_26"><div class="text-center staff-profile-image ratio ratio-1x1"><img src="/files/endorsed-candidates-photos/Rimga_Viskanta_600x750.jpg" alt="Rimga Viskanta" class="img-fluid rounded-circle" /></div>
