                                <div class="col-12 col-lg-8"><p><strong>Position:</strong> Mayor of Encinitas</p><div>Rimga Viskanta is a candidate for Mayor of Encinitas and has lived in the city for two decades, where she raised three children.<div><br></div><div>She previously served on the Encinitas Union School District Board from 2016 to 2020, including a term as Board President in 2020. She currently serves as Vice President of the San Dieguito Union High School District Board of Trustees, elected in 2022, and has twice served as Board President. In this role she helped bring electric school buses to the district, facilitated the formation of its first districtwide Sustainability Committee, and is pushing for electrification measures in the district’s facilities master plan update process.</div><div><br></div><div>She holds a Bachelor of Arts in Environmental Sciences from the University of Virginia and a Master of Public Administration from the University of Southern California. She served as Senior Management Analyst for the City of Solana Beach, where her sustainability work included overseeing the update and implementation of the City’s climate action plan, citywide organics recycling, building decarbonization reach codes, and native habitat initiatives.</div><div><br></div><div>As Mayor, Rimga will prioritize climate readiness, safer streets, and smarter growth. That means adopting an updated Climate Action Plan for Encinitas, building mobility infrastructure, installing more solar power on city facilities, and protecting open spaces and rewilding as much public and private property as possible. She is honored to have the Sierra Club’s support and asks for your vote on November 3.</div></div></div></div></div></div>
