                                <div class="col-12 col-lg-8"><p><strong>Position:</strong> Encinitas City Council, District 4</p><div>Brad Lefkowits’s connection to the Sierra Club began before he was born: his parents met at a Sierra Club singles event in the late 1970s. Their shared love of the outdoors became part of the family he grew up in and the values he now hopes to bring to the Encinitas City Council.<div><br></div><div>Brad is a small-business owner, husband, and father of two children who attend Encinitas public schools. His work as a landscape designer focuses on sustainable landscapes, climate-appropriate planting, native plants, water conservation, rainwater capture, and responsible stormwater management. Working throughout the region has given him firsthand experience with the environmental and infrastructure challenges facing our communities.</div><div><br></div><div>Since 2023, Brad has served on the City of Encinitas Urban Forest Advisory Committee, including one year as chair. He has worked to improve the city’s tree policies, protect mature trees, expand the urban canopy where appropriate, and promote safer, more resilient landscapes in areas facing serious wildfire risk.</div><div><br></div><div>Brad is running for City Council to restore Encinitas’s environmental leadership. His priorities include protecting open space, keeping beaches and waterways clean, updating and implementing the city’s Climate Action Plan, improving walking and biking infrastructure, and making thoughtful land-use decisions that align growth with infrastructure.</div><div><br></div><div>Brad believes environmental leadership must be practical, forward-looking, and grounded in science. He will bring his professional experience, collaborative approach, and deep commitment to the natural environment to every decision at City Hall.</div></div></div></div></div></div>
