                                <div class="col-12 col-lg-8"><p><strong>Position:</strong> Encinitas Union School District Board of Trustees</p><div>Jillian is a working mother and a special education parent whose daughter attends La Costa Heights Elementary in the Encinitas Union School District. She has spent over two years doing the work to prepare for the role of school board trustee. She has attended more Encinitas Union School District public meetings than any other community member — budget adoptions, facilities reviews, city coordination meetings and late-night controversies. She serves on the Citizens’ Bond Oversight Committee for Measure Z, the district’s $158.3 million facilities bond, and as a parent representative on the Special Education Parent Council.<div><br></div><div>She has more than 20 years experience in nonpartisan governmental policy across Washington D.C., London, and Brussels. That experience is not glamorous and entails sitting through hearings, reading legislation and picking out the language to improve to get the right result. These skills are what are going to make her a valuable school board member.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Attention to details is also what meaningful environmental commitments require. EUSD named environmental stewardship a priority in 2009. Since then the District has developed effective programs but they will continue to deliver results only if someone on the board is paying attention year after year, through budget cycles and board turnover. Jillian will be that person.</div><div><br></div><div>Jillian Cocayne ~ Does the work. For Our Students.</div></div></div></div></div></div>
