arents of EUSD, and the parent of three children in EUSD.</div><div><br></div><div>On the board, I will work to make climate a standing part of how EUSD governs its nine campuses: cleaner, more efficient buildings paid for through Measure Z, safer routes to school, healthier grounds and food, and stable funding for the environmental education programs under threat in this election. I will work to create a district climate action plan.</div><div><br></div><div>I am proud to be endorsed by the Teachers of Encinitas, Representative Mike Levin, Senator Catherine Blakespear, and Assemblymember Tasha Boerner. I’m especially proud to have the support of the Sierra Club.</div></div></div></div></div></div>
