                                <div class="col-12 col-lg-8"><p><strong>Position:</strong> San Dieguito Union High School District Area 3</p><div>As the daughter of a public-school teacher, mother of three school-aged children, and 16-year resident of Del Mar, I am invested in our schools and community. I volunteer in the classroom, am active with the PTA, and have regularly attended local School Board meetings for more than three years, giving me valuable insight into how effective governance supports student success. I’m entering my fourth year as a Director for Del Mar Union’s district-wide foundation, working collaboratively with district staff, teachers, and parents to raise funds for DMUSD STEAM+ teachers.&nbsp;<div><br></div><div>Sixteen years ago, I became a Court Appointed Special Advocate (CASA) advocating for the needs of foster children in court. I continue that advocacy by helping train new CASAs to work with biological parents toward reunification. My husband and I earned our foster license and adopted two of our children. My experience with the foster system has deepened my commitment to ensuring that every child’s voice is heard, and their needs are met.</div><div><br></div><div>My work as a mechanical engineer designing medical devices has taught me collaboration, problem-solving, and responsible stewardship of resources. I will bring that same mindset to the Board, including a commitment to sustainability and thoughtful, environmentally responsible decisions that protect our schools and&nbsp; community for future generations. I appreciate SDUHSD’s decision to increase its reserve percentage and its history of successful audits. I will support steadily increasing the reserve while balancing the needs of all students and staff.</div></div></div></div></div></div>
