1000
 is running for School Board in the San Dieguito Union High School District, Area 5. As a public high school teacher with 20 years of experience, Justin holds nine different teaching credentials and earned his National Board Teacher Certification as an expat in Ciudad de México D.F. Moodie was sent to China on a Fulbright-Hays fellowship to collaborate with their educators in the development of cross-cultural curricula. Later, Justin earned his Administrative Services credential and an M.A. in Educational Leadership at UC Berkeley, with a focus on social justice. Serving with the CA Department of Education, Justin worked to create the new state standards for Visual and Performing Arts, published in 2019. Justin was awarded a Grosvenor Teacher Fellowship by the National Geographic Society and joined Lindblad Expeditions on an expedition to explore Antarctica in February 2023. Followed by a collaboration with the Geophysics Department at U. Maine and an expedition to Mongolia sponsored by the Tang Center for Silk Road Studies at UC Berkeley, Justin has established himself as an educator sought out for international and outdoors experience from which to build new learning&nbsp; opportunities for students around exploration.&nbsp;It was no&nbsp; surprise when Justin became a CA Certified Naturalist. And, in November 2025, his extraordinary efforts were recognized when the California Association of Art Educators granted Justin the award for Secondary Art Educator of Year. Justin currently lives with his family in San Diego, CA and teaches CTE Photography at Oceanside High School.</div></div></div></div></div>
