                                <div class="col-12 col-lg-8"><p><strong>Position:</strong> Solana Beach City Council District 3</p><div>As a Solana Beach City Councilmember for the past two terms, I am proud of our leadership on environmental issues.&nbsp; We were the first to ban smoking on beaches, single use plastic bags, and polystyrene containers. We were also the first City in San Diego County to form a Community Choice Energy (CCE) program and now there are 13 cities and the county of San Diego in one of the two CCEs. I have been a founding member of both Solana Energy Alliance and Clean Energy Alliance, which recently celebrated its fifth anniversary.&nbsp;<div><br></div><div>Protecting our beaches and coastline is another top priority.&nbsp; We successfully completed a beach sand replenishment project and secured federal funding for future sand replenishment for the next 50 years.&nbsp; As Chair of the SANDAG Shoreline Preservation Working Group, I worked with all of the coastal cities to develop a long-ter
1000
m regional sand replenishment strategy to protect our entire fragile coastline.&nbsp;&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Keeping our beaches clean and protecting our ocean are equally important.&nbsp; We passed an ordinance opposing offshore drilling, installed a beach litter pickup station, and&nbsp;added a Beach Borrow Toy Box, helping prevent beach toys from entering the ocean while giving future visitors the opportunity to reuse them.</div><div><br></div><div>Looking ahead, I will prioritize implementation of our City’s Climate Action Plan strategies and actions to reduce Greenhouse gas emissions and build a more sustainable future.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Protecting our environment is good for our quality of life and good for our local economy and businesses.</div></div></div></div></div></div>
