                                <div class="col-12 col-lg-8"><p><strong>Position:</strong> Vista City Council</p><div>My name is Dan O’Donnell, and I’m running for re-election to the Vista City Council. Since being elected in 2022, I’ve fought to protect what makes Vista livable: pushing back against developers who put profit over community, securing new parkland and green space, expanding our tree canopy, and banning pesticides in our parks to protect the families and wildlife that use them every day. I’ve supported greater mobility so residents have real alternatives to sitting in traffic, and I’ve worked to update aging infrastructure so it can meet the demands of a changing climate.<div><br></div><div>I’ve also worked to keep Vista affordable and walkable, because sound land use is climate policy too. Sprawl and displacement push people into longer commutes and higher emissions; building thoughtfully within our existing footprint doesn’t.</div><div><br></div><div>The work isn’t finished. As your Council member, I’ll keep showing up, keep listening, and keep fighting for a Vista that’s greener, more resilient, and more livable for the next generation. Now is not the time to take a step backward.</div></div></div></div></div></div>
