                                <div class="col-12 col-lg-8"><p><strong>Position:</strong> Poway City Council District 3</p><div>Bob Walder is a retired healthcare professional, biomedical engineer, business leader, and longtime community volunteer. He has lived in Poway since 1998 and built his career around healthcare, innovation, leadership, and service.<div><br></div><div>Bob began his career as a biomedical engineer and later became a cardiovascular perfusionist and Physician Assistant. He worked for Abbott Laboratories in its Hospital Products Division and was involved in the development and commercialization of healthcare technologies. He helped establish Digirad Imaging Solutions, a nuclear imaging company, and contributed to the commercialization of TearLab, an ophthalmic point-of-care diagnostic company.</div><div><br></div><div>After retiring from TearLab, Bob returned to clinical practice, specializing in ECMO and caring for critically ill patients requiring advanced cardiopulmonary support.</div><div><br></div><div>Community service has remained central to Bob’s life. He&nbsp;volunteers with the San Diego Police Department and serves as an administrator for the Rancho Bernardo Retired Senior Volunteer Patrol (RSVP), coordinating operations and participating in&nbsp; community patrol.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Bob’s priorities are Public Safety, supporting properly staffed and responsive police, fire, and emergency services; Responsible Development, ensuring growth fits Poway and protects neighborhoods, infrastructure, and quality of life; Fiscal Responsibility, ensuring taxpayer dollars are spent wisely; and Preserve Poway, protecting open space, hillsides, ridgelines, rural character, and the community identity that makes Poway special.</div></div></div></div></div></div>
