                                <div class="col-12 col-lg-8"><p><strong>Position:</strong> Mayor of Vista</p><div>Kenneth is a Latino community activist, environmental ally, Vista resident, and San Diego State University alumni. He is running for mayor of Vista to protect and expand the city’s green spaces. He believes that undeveloped land should be used as nature preserves, open spaces, or parks, not for development projects. He will protect the county’s MSCP habitat by ensuring the city collaborates with the county to prevent urban growth in these areas. He will also expand dedicated public land where possible.<div><br></div><div>Kenneth recognizes the global climate crisis as a real and growing problem. He will ensure the city expands and fully funds its climate action plan to create green jobs and help local businesses transition to green energy.</div><div><br></div><div>He plans to strengthen green transportation options by expanding and protecting bus and bike lanes and light rail projects. He will work to plant trees along city sidewalks and reduce Vista’s emissions by investing in public transportation and building a walkable, bikeable city.</div><div><br></div><div>He is running a grassroots, corporate-free campaign and takes no money from developers, corporations, or law enforcement. Therefore, his decisions on land use and the environment will be made without outside influence. Kenneth recognizes that the fight for the environment and the fight for working people are one and the same and that the Green New Deal must reach our most vulnerable neighborhoods first.</div></div></div></div></div></div>
