                                <div class="col-12 col-lg-8"><p><strong>Position:</strong> Helix Water District Board Division 2</p><div>Beth Damsky, L.Ac. is an elected official, serving on the Board of Directors of Helix Water District in San Diego County. An environmental scientist, she served on the Environmental Sustainability Commission of La Mesa CA from 2017 to 2022, with her last 3 years as its Chair. Andrea Beth is also a National Board-Certified Acupuncturist.<div><br></div><div>Climate change, environmental activism, drought, food insecurity, racial justice, and equity are among the many issues Andrea Beth champions. At age 11, she staffed Baldwin’s Efforts to Salvage Trash (BEST), one of our nation’s first recycling centers in Baldwin, NY. Andrea Beth has been involved in feminist politics, LGBTQ+ activism, AIDS issues, abortion rights, and electoral campaign work over the last 50+ years. In addition to her position on the Helix Water District, she is also a Commissioner appointed to the California Commission on the State of Hate.</div></div></div></div></div></div>
